{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/GauravGoyalAI/status/2108738730127397286","id":"2108738730127397286","text":"MCP in Gen AI — Explained Simply!\n\nAI models are becoming more powerful, but their real potential comes when they can interact with tools, databases, APIs, files, and external data.\n\nThat’s where MCP (Model Context Protocol) comes in. 🤖🔌\n\nThis infographic breaks down:\n\n🔹 MCP Host — The AI application or agent\n🔹 MCP Client — Connects the host with MCP servers\n🔹 MCP Server — Provides tools, data, and resources\n🔹 Tool Calls — Let AI invoke external capabilities in a standardized way\n🔹 Real-world examples — Databases, search, APIs, vector databases & enterprise systems\n\n👉 In simple terms: MCP provides a standardized way for AI applications to connect with and use external capabilities.\n\n📌 Save this as a quick MCP reference.\n📲 Follow @gauravgoyalai for more Gen AI & AI Engineering explainers.\n\n#MCP #ModelContextProtocol #GenAI #GenerativeAI #AIAgents AgenticAI AIEngineering LLM RAG ArtificialIntelligence MachineLearning AI","raw_text":{"text":"MCP in Gen AI — Explained Simply!\n\nAI models are becoming more powerful, but their real potential comes when they can interact with tools, databases, APIs, files, and external data.\n\nThat’s where MCP (Model Context Protocol) comes in. 🤖🔌\n\nThis infographic breaks down:\n\n🔹 MCP Host — The AI application or agent\n🔹 MCP Client — Connects the host with MCP servers\n🔹 MCP Server — Provides tools, data, and resources\n🔹 Tool Calls — Let AI invoke external capabilities in a standardized way\n🔹 Real-world examples — Databases, search, APIs, vector databases & enterprise systems\n\n👉 In simple terms: MCP provides a standardized way for AI applications to connect with and use external capabilities.\n\n📌 Save this as a quick MCP reference.\n📲 Follow @gauravgoyalai for more Gen AI & AI Engineering explainers.\n\n#MCP #ModelContextProtocol #GenAI #GenerativeAI #AIAgents AgenticAI AIEngin